Open Vanilla 0051: Boss Fights self-test, test accounts and a robust waiting line.

Owner, 2026-10-23: "robustly test the queue, the waiting line, ... go in, kill the boss, end, and refresh
yourself ... your own two accounts to test every feature itself". Everything below is off unless
OpenVanilla.BossFights.SelfTest = 1 (hetzner/bossfights_check.sh sets it on the Modes server only).

- Test accounts: OpenVanilla.BossFights.TestAccounts ("BFTEST*": names, ids or a PREFIX*). A test character is
  in Boss Fights from its first login (Duels' hangout code leaves it alone), queues in a pool of its own
  (never matched with players, no role rule), may pick the run's size (q onyxia size=2), and its runs stay off
  bossfights_now, the live counts and the boards (bossfights_result.test = 1, realm/bossfights SQL).
- Test commands (test accounts only): test state (one key=value line with the mode, hangout, waiting line,
  run, copy, map, tiers, aura, health, world buffs, consumables, level, faction), test kill (every encounter
  left in the run: its boss killed by the player, so the script, loot and encounter credit run as in a real
  kill), test wipe, test revive, test out (a step past the fence), test reset (progress, test results, lock,
  ticket, raid save; at once, so the next state reads it).
- Everyone: the waiting line (q,<raid>,<tier>,<queued>,<waited>,<position>,<size>,<still needed>; chat
  "Waiting line: N of M"), and leaving a run refreshes the player in the hangout (alive, full health and
  mana, the run's world buffs gone, cooldowns ready). The tier aura is read again 5 s after a clear or a
  reset (the progress row is written asynchronously, so the first read could miss it).
- BossFightsSelfTest.h: the pure parts (test accounts, the queue's words, the state line), tested by
  realm/bossfights/tests/test_selftest.cpp.

